      {
        "id": 24630,
        "name": "awmiller",
        "username": "awmiller",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/awmiller/{size}/2243_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-12-19T01:46:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Third game also ended in victory for our conquering heroes! Voss on Mars was super tough. Our heroes were Haka (me), Tempest (my room mate), and The Visionary (my wife). We slugged in out, only surviving a Forced Deployment onslaught due to The Visionary having the highest HP and being in a cocoon so that the damage didn’t finish us off before we could retaliate.</p>\n<p>This was of course followed up by a Rampage that killed all of the minions and fueled the Savage Mana bomb that eventually did Voss in. (36 damage!!!) Very exciting and close contest with the heroes barely besting the Conquering Warlord. Tempest did his fair share, and his Cleansing Downpour kept us all in the fight.</p>\n<p>Haka’s Haka of Restoration and Vitality Surges were absolutely necessary as I took the bulk of the initial damage and was down to 3 hp when a well timed Meteor Storm stopped all Voss’s damage long enough for me to get back into double digits.</p>\n<p>Overall, it was a true slobber-knocker of a fight and I can’t wait until we get a chance to attack Dawn in the Ruins of Atlantis later this week!</p>\n<p>(Also, we are thinking of trying to take on Omnitron in the Mars base with Bunker, Absolute Zero, and the Wraith just to see if that makes him into a challenge)</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
